      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Of course, a major downside of retroactive funding is that often, grantees need the money before they can start their project, to pay for salaries (their own or employees) or otherwise cover costs. My favorite solution to this are impact certificates, where investors can directly fund projects they expect to later earn retroactive payouts.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Of course, a major downside of retroactive funding is that often, grantees need the money before they can start their project, to pay for salaries (their own or employees) or otherwise cover costs. My favorite solution to this are impact certificates, where investors can directly fund projects they expect to later earn retroactive payouts.",
